vernments the u.s. in  order to operate has to raise revenue as  to tax right so these don't have taxing  power so they have to generate revenue  as organizations in order to sustain  themselves so how do they do that where  are the sources of revenue that are  sustainable for these organizations in  the future right now a lot of money  comes from government development  agencies or us foundations are very  heavily involved in supporting some  programs have more money from licensing  fees for their labels so that will be a  big question to how that plays out okay  very interesting thank you for being  here with us today you're welcome it was  a pleasure thank you yeah for more  information about professor alt please  visit our website at yale edu slash  mcmillan report be sure to join us again  for another episode of the macmillan  report made possible through funding  from the Whitney and Betty Macmillan  Center for International and area  studies at Yale  you
 

